gold and the BFD linker both link a program whose `-o` basename is `ld-new`
(ld/ from bin_PROGRAMS, gold/ from noinst_PROGRAMS). The engine's link-capture
sidecar is keyed on that basename, last writer wins, so the two clobber each
other's captured object list. Rename gold's program (automake prefix
`ld_new_` and the `ld-new$(EXEEXT)` file) to `ld-gold`; the flake's `linkName`
maps it back to the upstream name `ld.gold`. gold is noinst and the self-fold
replaces its install, so nothing depends on the old name. The bootstrap refs to
the top-level `$(abs_top_builddir)/ld-new` carry no $(EXEEXT) and stay.

